Write readable Python source only, no semicolons. Function diagnose(record,entries). Imports copy.deepcopy and matching.match_features. names set entry canonical_name casefold. expected list original record.features whose label first element casefold is in names. masked=deepcopy(record), masked.features retains features whose labels are NOT in names. predicted list from match_features(masked,entries) with status new and confidence High confidence. For each predicted hit h: name=h['entry']['canonical_name'];loc=h['location']. If any expected f with label casefold same name and f.location==loc, skip. Otherwise append dict(name=name,location=str(loc),closest=[dict(location=str(f.location),overlap=len(set(loc)&set(f.location))/max(len(loc),len(f.location))) for f in expected if same name casefold]). Return this list. Under35 lines. Actual schema exactly as stated. No IO, no placeholders, no main, no separate implementations of matching.
